From: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 11:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] bl_common: zero a rejected image with zeromem

When an image fails authentication, load_auth_image_recursive() wipes
it with zero_normalmem(), which uses DC ZVA and works only on normal
memory. MediaTek's BL2 runs with the MMU off, so the wipe faults and
BL2 stops in the panic handler instead of returning -EAUTH. Use
zeromem(), which works with the MMU on or off.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MediaTek's BL2 runs with the MMU off]
Signed-off-by: Vladimir Skvortsov <vskvortsov@emcraft.com>
---
--- a/common/bl_common.c
+++ b/common/bl_common.c
@@ -194,9 +194,12 @@
 				 (void *)image_data->image_base,
 				 image_data->image_size);
 	if (rc != 0) {
-		/* Authentication error, zero memory and flush it right away. */
-		zero_normalmem((void *)image_data->image_base,
-			       image_data->image_size);
+		/*
+		 * Authentication error, zero memory and flush it right away.
+		 * zeromem, not zero_normalmem: BL2 may run with the MMU off.
+		 */
+		zeromem((void *)image_data->image_base,
+			image_data->image_size);
 		flush_dcache_range(image_data->image_base,
 				   image_data->image_size);
 		return -EAUTH;
